{"dog":{"age_group":"young","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Medium mixed breed","breed_primary":"Medium Mixed Breed Cross","description_text":"This pet is available only through ACC New Hope partners. To adopt or foster, please complete the pre-screener form below. Inquiries sent directly to ACC will not receive a response.\n\nPre-Screener Form\n\nKing Biscuit was rehomed due to the behaviors he was presented in his original home. His previous owner stated that there were two dog fights and a bite incident that occurred in the home. The bite incident broke skin and resulted in bruising on the owner's leg. While in care, King has been observed to be highly fearful. Noted to have a tense body and low tail. Due to the detailed behavior, we recommend an experienced adult only, single pet home that makes no trips to the dog park.\n\nWhat my friends at ACC say about me:\n\nMy history is a mystery and my friends here do not know much about me yet!\n\nI can be slow to adjust to new environments. I prefer to take things at my own pace.\n\nI would do best in a home without very tiny humans, although I could be open to older human children once I meet them.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=3%2C16&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=14&searchType=4&animalid=205072","id":"967f76275c54345938dd85156fa43f4d","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/fb0a81c1ad04469ba38ed81a420ae545-1787511216-1787511232-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/232fa144e50d4e6891e5850838ecd996-1787511216-1787511216-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/efc5a83d8c4d4d8b8706b26c5e151588-1786840969-1786840977-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/7c2d02d6538f4aeeb965bc8522e5c924-1786840969-1786840969-jpeg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/24c